1. Log in to the application using the **Dhanavel** user account and navigate to the **Edit User Details** functionality.
2. Modify the user's profile details and save the changes.
3. Capture the HTTP request associated with the **Edit User Details** functionality and observe that the profile is updated successfully.
4. After the profile update, attempt to log in again. Observe that the application displays a **"User record not authorized"** message, indicating that the record requires approval from a superior user before it can be used.
5. Despite the user record being in an unauthorized state, observe that the application still generates a valid JWT token upon authentication.
6. Use the previously captured HTTP request from the Edit User Details functionality and modify the operationalID parameter value from process to authorize.
7. Submit the modified request and observe that the **Dhanavel** user is able to authorize their own record successfully.
8. Log in to the application again and observe that the user is able to access the application successfully after self-authorizing the record.
